id: pm-lk0qhn
title: Preserve dependency kind constraints in rendered enum errors
description: GitHub #1223 shows create/update dependency kind validation has a precise parser message but rendered errors retain only generic invalid_argument_value guidance. Preserve the named field and accepted values through structured error context shared by CLI MCP and SDK without copying arbitrary rejected content into recovery instructions.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-08T16:15:39.497Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-08T21:58:01.159Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-08T21:58:00.475Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-08T21:58:00.475Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Invalid dependency kinds name the field and accepted values in structured required guidance; text and JSON are actionable; rejected updates preserve the item; the shared parser retains the same accepted vocabulary.
parent: pm-96h7
severity: low
repro_steps: "Run update with --dep id=<valid-id>,kind=relates_to and inspect required/next_steps in JSON error output."
resolution: "Preserved accepted dependency-kind constraints and concrete retry guidance through structured SDK errors and CLI text/JSON rendering, while retaining the canonical machine-readable kind key for create, addition and removal parsers."
expected_result: Invalid dependency kinds retain named accepted values and context.field=kind across every parser without changing item or history state.
actual_result: "Direct create, update-addition and dependency-removal parser assertions pass alongside real CLI text/JSON and unchanged-state regressions. Sixth-round verification: all 8622 tests in 653 files pass with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and zero uncovered statements, branches, functions and lines. All four TypeScript projects, the full quality:static gate, serialized docs/skills checks, and every linked test command pass. Both original clone profiles remain unchanged; the supplementary historical-table profile also passes. Final pushed-head CI, full platform matrix, review and preflight remain required before merge."
component: sdk/lifecycle
